PACKAGE DESCRIPTION:
idekern:  Linux kernel version 1.1.18, without SCSI support.
idekern:  
idekern:  A Linux kernel for computers that do not need SCSI support. If you 
idekern:  don't have SCSI, the advantage of using the idekern kernel is that 
idekern:  your machine will boot faster with a leaner kernel. See the file
idekern:  'idekern.log' for an exact list of included drivers. A short list:
idekern:  
idekern:  This kernel also has support for PPP, UMSDOS, CSLIP, Ethernet,
idekern:  Ftape, and the PS/2 style mouse (but not other busmouse types).
